auth {
  mode: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

tests {
  // Runs after EVERY request in this collection.
  test("the server answers 200 — GraphQL says everything with the body", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("the timing middleware tagged the response", function() {
    expect(res.getHeader("x-process-time-ms")).to.be.a("string");
  });
}

docs {
  # HR Skills GraphQL API

  Every request below points at one URL — `POST {{baseUrl}}/graphql` — and asks for a
  different slice of the same graph. Start the server first:

      cd fast-api-graphql
      uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload

  Then pick the **Local** environment (top right) and run the collection.

  ## The one habit to unlearn

  A GraphQL server answers **200** for a blocked candidate, a missing requisition and a
  rejected skill level alike. The status line stops carrying meaning, so every test here
  asserts on the *body*:

  - `errors` with `data: null` → the request was never valid. A bug in the client.
  - a `__typename` inside `data` → a domain outcome. The server working correctly.

  The folders are ordered so the collection can be run top to bottom against a freshly
  started server, and re-run without resetting it.
}
